  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist. The rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view exploration:** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` has 35 fields. The ones that matter here are `timestamp` (time field), `response` / `response.keyword` (status code, stored as a string), `extension.keyword` (file type), `clientip`, `bytes`, `geo.dest`, and `host`. I could not pull value distributions or the data's time range, because the API key is rejected by the Kibana Dev Console proxy and by ES directly. The panels and the rule therefore rely on field names and types, not on observed values.\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-f71e724a Web logs overview` (id `eff-f71e724a-web-logs-overview-1a69a414234f`), default time range last 7 days, six panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time by response code (bar, date histogram \u00d7 `response.keyword`)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Top requested file types (bar, `extension.keyword`)\n\n**Alert rule:** `EFF-f71e724a 5xx spike` (id `c24acb9d-3205-438c-9d41-2c97e8bd6e7f`), enabled.\n- Type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, looks back over a 5m window on `timestamp`.\n- Filter: `response.keyword` between `\"500\"` and `\"599\"`. This is a string range, which is correct for three-digit codes.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Tagged `EFF-f71e724a`.\n\nThe rule's status is still `pending` because it has not run yet. I have not confirmed that it evaluates without error. Since the sample data is static, it will probably not fire unless 5xx responses fall within the last 5 minutes.",
